# Mi Pad 2 test no-idle mode

Opt in with `sudo mp2-test-no-idle enable`; inspect with `status`; restore with
`disable`. The existing single system inhibitor blocks idle/sleep/lid handling.
GNOME power settings are saved and restored as before.

When a Denial session is available, its own `power.idleDpmsEnabled` is disabled
through the versioned native settings API. This is required even with the
system inhibitor active. The original boolean is saved privately in the desktop
user's state directory and restored on disable. Repeated enable preserves that
first restore value. Only this field is edited, with expected_revision CAS;
concurrent changes/errors retain the restore record and fail visibly.

Authentication, idle lock, physical power-key action and Denial suspend policy
are not changed. This does not unlock the desktop or repeatedly inject input.
Denial's persisted setting survives reboot. `status` checks the native setting,
not merely whether the inhibitor process exists. Restoring a saved Denial value
requires its session to be available; no offline blind settings-file overwrite
is performed. Without Denial and without a saved restore record, the existing
GNOME-only path remains supported. No extra service or watchdog is created.

No Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, display scale, kernel selection or Secure Boot changes.
